use the structure <span class=\"strong\">prefer to + (verb)</span> or <span class=\"strong\">prefer + (verb-ing)</span> to say what you prefer in general.<br>   The structure after <span class=\"strong\">prefer </span> can be:<br>  <br>I prefer something to something else.<br>  <span class=\"italic\">Example: I prefer swimming to running.<br></span>  <br> I prefer to do something rather than (do) something else.<br>  <span class=\"italic\">Example: I prefer to walk rather than run.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't like jogging. <span class=\"strong\">I prefer</span> to go for long walks."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sometimes, <span class=\"strong\">I prefer</span> to sit at a park and people watch."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Colosseum"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a famous ancient Roman structure "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did I also say that I was visiting the Colosseum in Rome too?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you talk about tourist activities."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "local "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who lives in the same area for a long time "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I like to meet the local people."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "people watch"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "spending time in one place watching people  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sometimes, I prefer to sit in a park and people watch."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents":